#: fm1companion/studio.py:83
msgid "The twin computes without a CPU limit: under overload the device drops voices (overload shedding), the twin never does. Floating-point parts (FM6 voice pairs, which CPU1 computes on the device, effect filters) may differ in the last bits (inaudible). No BLE, no USB host, no firmware update in the twin. The resource arena has the size of the host tests (at least that of the device). Stems come from several runs with muted tracks (track solo, with its share of the shared effects); because of the master dynamics the sum of the stems does not exactly match the mix."
msgstr ""

#: fm1companion/studio.py:148
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Your FM-1 runs M-VAVE's original firmware {device}. Its code is not open, so there is no twin of it: the studio runs M-VAVE's open firmware FM1 Open {twin} instead – with the same 128 factory DX7 voices (taken from the V15 package), but a different firmware: its own operation, 8 tracks and 16 projects, its own sample bank, and the open engine of M-VAVE's browser simulator instead of the device's. Sound and functions may differ. The original firmware has no backup protocol: nothing can be fetched from it or written back to it."
msgstr ""

#: fm1companion/studio.py:168
